WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:20.664
Morning finally came, and Aladdin was waiting in his grand, new clothes.

2
00:00:22.045 --> 00:00:26.368
When Magrib arrived, they both hurried down the street of crooked houses.

3
00:00:26.388 --> 00:00:30.151
"Where are we going today, Uncle?"

4
00:00:30.571 --> 00:00:31.232
asked Aladdin.

5
00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.153
"What will I see that I have never seen before?"

6
00:00:34.173 --> 00:00:38.776
"Ah, my boy, you must be patient," answered Magrib.

7
00:00:40.116 --> 00:00:41.817
"We will see wonderful things!

8
00:00:42.538 --> 00:00:43.818
Amazing treasures!"

9
00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:48.781
The magician had never been so happy.

10
00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.722
This was the day he had waited for!

11
00:00:52.823 --> 00:00:56.645
He laughed and embraced Aladdin—just like an uncle would.

12
00:00:58.006 --> 00:01:01.688
A very old and very high wall stood around the city.

13
00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:06.007
When the two travelers came to the wall, Aladdin stopped.

14
00:01:06.027 --> 00:01:11.452
"I have never gone beyond the wall," he said quietly.

15
00:01:11.472 --> 00:01:18.618
"It’s only one step farther for you to see a new world," said Magrib as he took Aladdin’s

16
00:01:18.658 --> 00:01:23.282
hand. They walked through the gate and left the city behind.

17
00:01:23.302 --> 00:01:31.688
"Now we will stroll in the most beautiful gardens," said Magrib.

18
00:01:31.728 --> 00:01:37.532
Everywhere, they saw roses, fragrant herbs, fruit trees, and flowering vines.

19
00:01:39.634 --> 00:01:44.057
Sparkling water bubbled from brass fountains shaped like lions.

20
00:01:44.077 --> 00:01:47.499
"Do these sights please you?"

21
00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:48.760
asked Magrib.

22
00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.882
"I have never seen such things before!"

23
00:01:52.342 --> 00:01:53.023
said Aladdin.

24
00:01:53.043 --> 00:01:55.505
"Everything pleases me!"

25
00:01:58.967 --> 00:02:02.342
Now, my young friends, Aladdin was very happy.

26
00:02:03.463 --> 00:02:05.485
But he was very hungry too.

27
00:02:06.846 --> 00:02:09.909
Walking with his uncle had made his stomach growl.

28
00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:15.434
Zeba hadn't packed any food for his trip, and he wondered what he would eat.

29
00:02:16.655 --> 00:02:17.736
He shouldn't have worried.

30
00:02:19.598 --> 00:02:25.243
Magrib reached into the sleeve of his robe and pulled out a sesame cookie and a handful of

31
00:02:25.323 --> 00:02:32.761
figs. They ate under a big tree, and Magrib told Aladdin stories about his life in Egypt.

32
00:02:34.062 --> 00:02:37.124
Some of the stories were true, and some were not.

33
00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:42.028
But in a short time, the magician was eager to travel farther.

34
00:02:46.272 --> 00:02:47.313
now," he said.

35
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.695
"The best is yet to come!"

36
00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:55.820
And so they walked on—from garden to garden—until there were no more gardens.

37
00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.783
Aladdin saw that the land was no longer fresh and green.

38
00:03:01.964 --> 00:03:04.406
The ground was baked brown by the sun.

39
00:03:06.348 --> 00:03:08.570
Magrib walked faster and faster.

40
00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:13.994
Aladdin had to run to keep up, and he stumbled on the hot stones.

41
00:03:14.014 --> 00:03:16.977
"I am so tired, Uncle!

42
00:03:17.437 --> 00:03:18.738
May I please rest?"

43
00:03:19.099 --> 00:03:19.559
he said.

44
00:03:19.579 --> 00:03:22.342
"No!" answered the magician.

45
00:03:22.362 --> 00:03:23.963
"This is the way.

46
00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:24.884
Walk quickly!"

47
00:03:26.508 --> 00:03:27.848
"But where are we going, Uncle?

48
00:03:29.089 --> 00:03:31.349
There are no more gardens, only bare hills.

49
00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.831
If it is far, I cannot go on, and we must turn back."

50
00:03:35.851 --> 00:03:39.652
"It is not too far," answered Magrib.

51
00:03:39.672 --> 00:03:43.333
"And soon, I will show you the most beautiful garden you can imagine!"

52
00:03:44.633 --> 00:03:46.333
But they did not come to a garden.

53
00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:50.074
They came to the bottom of a high, rocky hill.

54
00:03:50.094 --> 00:03:55.816
"Now, Aladdin, you may sit," said the magician, his eyes glowing.

55
00:03:56.876 --> 00:03:58.658
"We have reached the place I was seeking."

56
00:04:00.459 --> 00:04:03.722
Aladdin was glad to rest, but he was excited too.

57
00:04:03.742 --> 00:04:08.205
"Collect some dry sticks for a fire," ordered Magrib.

58
00:04:08.225 --> 00:04:13.990
"Yes, Uncle," said Aladdin as he jumped up and gathered some twigs into a pile.

59
00:04:16.152 --> 00:04:20.916
When the fire was burning brightly, Magrib pulled a silver box from his sleeve.

60
00:04:22.277 --> 00:04:25.880
He opened it and took out a pinch of some sweet-smelling powder.

61
00:04:27.232 --> 00:04:30.893
He spoke strange words that Aladdin did not understand.

62
00:04:30.913 --> 00:04:32.994
"Magic words?"

63
00:04:33.494 --> 00:04:34.394
Aladdin wondered.

64
00:04:36.355 --> 00:04:39.175
Then Magrib tossed the powder into the fire.

65
00:04:40.356 --> 00:04:44.377
Within moments, the sky turned dark and roared with thunder.

66
00:04:45.597 --> 00:04:49.118
The ground shook, and rocks tumbled around Aladdin's head.

67
00:04:50.598 --> 00:04:53.799
Suddenly, the earth split open right in front of him!

68
00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:56.420
Aladdin screamed.
